# ros-docker-scripts

The repo houses scripts to run Robot Operating System (ROS) dockers.  There are several versions available:

| Branch | Notes |
|---|---|
| main | Just this README and license file. |
| foxy | Built and tested using ROS Foxy and Ubuntu 22.04LTS. |
| jazzy | Built and tested using ROS Jazzy and Ubuntu 24.04LTS. |
| kilted | Built and tested using ROS Kilted and Ubuntu 24.04LTS. |
| jazzy-wayland | Built and tested using ROS Jazzy and Ubuntu 26.04LTS. |
| lyrical-wayland | Built and tested using ROS Jazzy and Ubuntu 26.04LTS. |

Most branches have two Docker versions.  Each version has a `README.md` file that explains how to use the scripts.

1. The `docker` scripts are intended for text only dockers suitable for building, running and testing code.  Graphics do work but are not accelerated.
2. The `nvidia_docker` scripts do the same as that `docker` scripts and also allow the use of the NVIDIA GPU and its CUDA cores for simulation in `Gazebo` and `RViz2`.

Please feel free to use this repo for your own projects.  I often start a new ROS project repo, copy the the Docker scripts into the new repo and modify as needed.

